SM(615,{"n":"Revelation 4.8-6.17","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Revelation 4.8-6.17.mp3","d":2640.6,"s":[[0.24,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.96,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in Biblical Studies, and is an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[20.4,"So now we're gonna read about what said Kerovine are uh are doing."],[28.88,"Verse 8. The four living creatures, each having six wings, were full of eyes around and within."],[36.8,"And they do not rest day or night saying, Holy, holy, holy, Lord God Almighty, who was and is and is to come."],[46.24,"Um that probably sounds familiar."],[50.14,"Um, this is not the first place it appears with the Bible either."],[53.02,"This is based on what they're singing in uh Isaiah's vision."],[58.08,"So um the reason they're covered with eyes."],[63.25,"Eyes are talking about the power of vision, the power of sight and awareness of what's going on on the earth."],[69.19,"If these are the four cardinal points."],[71.89,"They're sort of over the whole earth."],[75.65,"Verse 9 Whenever the living creatures give glory and honor and thanks to him who sits on the throne, who lives forever and ever, the 24 elders fall down before him who sits on the throne and worship him who lives forever and ever, and cast their crowns before the throne, saying, You are worthy, O Lord, to receive glory and honor and power, for you created all things, and by your will they exist and were created."],[100.61,"Okay So there's sort of antiphonal uh worship going on, between the caravim and the humans."],[113.73,"Who are in God's throne room, back and forth."],[117.66,"And so remember, excuse me, right after St."],[121.9,"John went through the door into heaven, he said he was in the spirit."],[126.24,"He used that worship language that he was entering into the worship."],[129.84,"And so this is making uh a point that when we enter into the worship of God, that includes us here in Lafayette, Louisiana, on a Sunday morning or whatever."],[142.31,"We are joining the regularly scheduled worship of God already in progress."],[147.73,"That's going on in heaven day and night continuously."],[152.22,"We're like plugging in."],[156.03,"And that's true of everyone everywhere."],[160.25,"And so we're not only directly connected to what's going on in heaven, meaning to God, to the angels."],[166.97,"That's why we mention angels so much of the divine liturgy serving with us and worshiping with us, the saints."],[173.63,"But that also means everyone else worshiping everywhere else in the world, connected through there."],[181.49,"So every, especially the divine liturgy, but every worship service. is a manifestation of the unity of the church through time and space"],[194.14,"Through time and space."],[195.18,"And this is this is one of the reasons why I know there's a tradition among some of our people that after a loved one dies, they don't come to church for a while."],[205.66,"And I'm sorry."],[207.9,"That's one of the silliest traditions I've ever heard in my life."],[211.02,"Because your loved one who passed away is here at the church."],[215.42,"Every time we're worshiping."],[217.1,"ing If you stay home, you're staring stay away from your loved one who you missed."],[218.14,"Who you miss"],[224.66,"It's better you should be here where they are, and worshiping God with them."],[230.1,"And praying for them and with them."],[232.74,"Than at home being depressed."],[235.08,"And sad. So that's the reality."],[242.19,"So because again, the purpose of this is St."],[245.47,"John showing us the reality that we can't see from our point of view here on the ground."],[251.77,"This is part of that reality."],[254.01,"That when he was worshiping in that cave next to a salt mine, when he and the other Christians could sneak off to go worship God."],[263.4,"It wasn't just them huddled in a cave with some candles and some lamps."],[269.06,"They were part of this that's going on in heaven."],[275.6,"So it doesn't matter if your church is the biggest cathedral in the world."],[280.61,"They let you they let us reopen the Huggy of Sophia."],[283.9,"Or if it's a storefront or somebody's living room."],[287.28,"This is what we're connecting to, and we become a part of."],[291.28,"Chapter 5, verse 1."],[296.48,"So we've kind of got the scene set now."],[298.88,"Now the action is gonna start sort of unfolding."],[304.76,"And I saw in the right hand of him who sat on the throne a scroll written inside and on the back, sealed with seven seals."],[314.48,"Okay. So you usually wouldn't write on both sides of a scroll."],[321.42,"That's why it makes the point."],[322.46,"You'd write on like the the one side, and then you'd roll that up on the inside to protect the writing."],[326.88,"But this is written on both sides, but it's rolled up."],[329.84,"And then these are like wax seals."],[332.58,"That you'd put on it to seal it, and if someone and you have to break them, in order to open it, so you could tell whether it's been opened or not."],[345.71,"Verse 2. Then I saw a strong angel proclaiming with a loud voice, Who is worthy to open the scroll and to loose its seals?"],[354.83,"Okay. So the scroll is sitting in the right hand."],[358.67,"The one sitting on the throne, it's sealed"],[362.45,"The angel yells, Who's worthy to break the seals and open it?"],[368.69,"Verse 3, and no one in heaven or on the earth or under the earth was able to open the scroll or to look at it."],[375.65,"Okay. So heaven, earth, under the earth means the underworld."],[380.93,"Hades. You kind of figure none of them were going to be worthy."],[385.97,"But I guess thoroughness, you gotta check."],[388.99,"Um I wept much because no one was found worthy to open and read the scroll or to look at it."],[400.91,"But one of the elders said to me, and it doesn't say which one."],[404.15,"I wonder if he was talking to himself."],[409.43,"Do not weep."],[411.43,"Behold the lion of the tribe of Judah, the root of David, has prevailed to open the scroll and to loose its seven seals."],[419.75,"Okay. So he weeps because no one can open the scroll."],[424.79,"Find out what's in it."],[426.79,"He gets told by this elder, maybe himself, that he should not weep because there's this person, and these lion of the tribe of Judah referenced back to Genesis, one of the early prophecies of the Messiah, root of David, obviously mess you know, talking about the Messiah."],[443.83,"And notice that he's prevailed."],[446.31,"So he's accomplished this victory, and that's now going to allow him to open the seals."],[457.36,"But this is going to be the result of what he's accomplished."],[464.56,"Verse 6, and I looked, and behold, in the midst of the throne and of the four living creatures, and in the midst of the elders stood a lamb, as though it had been slain, having seven horns and seven eyes, which are the seven spirits of God sent out into all the earth."],[482.56,"Okay. So he looks back over to the throne."],[488.24,"Notice it's the same throne."],[490.78,"So this. figure, the lamb there, and Christ is identified as the Lamb of God in St"],[498.26,"John's gospel. So he's using the same symbolism."],[501.83,"The Lamb is there on the throne where the one who sat on the throne God was."],[508.87,"It says in the midst of all of these I pictured in the sort of in the middle of the thing."],[514.63,"No, remember, they're around the throne."],[516.87,"So the Lamb is on the throne in the midst of those."],[521.31,"You're right. My Bible says between the throne of the four living creatures."],[529.15,"Um, and so the lamb looks as if it's been slain."],[538.69,"So this is both the Messiah and its God."],[541.43,"And he's been slain."],[542.47,"This is very obviously talking about Christ."],[544.49,"Having died and been resurrected."],[547.13,"Christ after his resurrection, remember, still had the wounds, of his resurrection, as sort of the marks, of his of his victory."],[556.12,"Verse 7, then he came and took the scroll out of the right hand of him who sat on the throne."],[562.36,"Now, when he had taken the scroll, the four living creatures and the twenty-four elders fell down before the lamb, each having a harp, and golden bowls full of incense, which are the prayers of the saints."],[576.2,"Okay. So all the people we saw worshiping before, now all are worshiping the Lamb."],[588.74,"So we've got worship."],[590.5,"Again, another thing that he's God, that this is not someone other than God."],[598.66,"And here the harps do show up, I admit, but they're not being scrummed sitting on clouds."],[608.82,"And notice they have golden bowls full of incense, which are the prayers of the saints."],[613.86,"So notice what St"],[617.22,"John is saying here."],[619.22,"There are prayers from people on earth that are coming up before Christ through these saints who are in heaven."],[639.87,"So sometimes we get asked by some of our Protestant friends, where the stuff about praying to saints or praying with saints or asking saints to pray for us is in the Bible."],[652.51,"Well, here's one place."],[654.93,"The prayers of the saints are being offered before God by the saints in heaven."],[664.9,"And so you notice. there's no we're giving it, we're giving a picture here"],[670.62,"There's not like this is not the product of like a rational argument."],[675.51,"So you don't have St."],[676.71,"John saying, now, people, you can't approach God directly."],[680.63,"Or it's okay to approach Jesus directly."],[683.83,"You don't have to go through the same."],[685.21,"This is not like, we're just presented this picture."],[688.27,"Because remember, one of the themes we've got going on in the background here from chapter four that's been established is this unity of the whole church in prayer."],[697.73,"So we would expect, if we in worship are united with the heavenly worship, for us to be praying for them, them to be praying for us."],[707.03,"We're all praying for each other."],[708.47,"Like we're all connected we're all praying for each other."],[708.66,"Well, how does that work"],[711.52,"So this isn't a weird thing that we then have to break."],[714.8,"Why do we have to do it that way?"],[716.08,"Well, how do we"],[716.86,"Those questions don't even really make sense with what we're being presented here."],[724.2,"They're questions we might have."],[726.74,"Also doesn't make them valid."],[728.36,"But that's we might have, because, but but they're they're questions that proceed from a way of thinking that is kind of foreign to what's going on here in the scriptures."],[739.41,"It's a way of thinking that says, well, you know, maybe that's okay, but why do I have to do it?"],[748.47,"Whereas St. John is painting us this beautiful. picture of the unity of the church"],[752.83,"And you know, it's like, well, but do I have to?"],[755.47,"I mean, can I like not do that and just do the right?"],[759.87,"Like, that's a different, that's a whole different approach, to worship in reality than what we have here."],[768.53,"So then verse 9, and they sang a new song saying, You are worthy to take the scroll and open its seals, for you were slain and have redeemed us to God by your blood, out of every tribe and tongue and people and nation."],[784.39,"So this is making abundantly clear how it is that there's now the humans up there."],[790.73,"They straight out say it."],[792.81,"Christ redeemed them, by his blood."],[794.09,"And redeemed means exactly what redeemed sounds like"],[800.02,"Like when you redeem a coupon, when you redeem it means you buy back."],[808.23,"Um excuse me."],[811.11,"And in this case, it's specifically buying out of slavery."],[816.23,"Um so we tend to, as much as I wrote my dissertation about it, we tend to, when we think about Christ and his blood and his death, we tend to think about atonement and the Day of Atonement all the time."],[831.29,"But that's not the way the Bible usually, the New Testament usually talks about Christ's death and resurrection."],[838.29,"What usually talks about his death and resurrection is Passover."],[844.13,"Exhibit A, here he's presented as a lamb."],[848.23,"You have goats at the Day of Atonement."],[851.43,"You have a lamb at Passover."],[854.2,"And Passover is very clearly what happens at Passover."],[862.44,"The people of God are freed from slavery."],[868.29,"God renders judgment on the gods of Egypt and sets his people free from slavery."],[873.09,"That's what happens on Passover."],[875.3,"And that's how Christ's death and resurrection is being presented here."],[878.82,"That's the redemption. language"],[882.3,"In this world, people were slaves, slaves to sin, slaves to death, slaves to the demonic powers."],[889.58,"Christ came and died and rose again and through that set them free, brought them into heaven."],[899.1,"And they're giving praise for that."],[900.86,"And notice every tribe and tongue and people and nation."],[908.78,"So it's not just about Israelites getting set free from Egypt and the Egyptian gods."],[916.46,"It's about the Egyptians getting set free from Egypt."],[919.52,"It's about the Romans getting set free from Egypt."],[922.16,"It's about the even the dreaded. 19th century Germans getting set free from the right"],[929.08,"Um. So everyone."],[934.36,"Verse 10, and have made us kings and priests to our God, and we shall reign on the earth."],[941.48,"So remember, they were sitting in thrones already."],[945.02,"So God is, or Christ is sharing his rule over the world."],[949.9,"Now that he's taken rule over the world, he's sharing it now with them."],[954.6,"And so they're now reigning with Christ."],[957.48,"This is going to be important when we get to Revelation 20."],[960.85,"Because this is something that's happening here."],[962.93,"Notice also, they're kings and what?"],[966.13,"Priests. ests So what do what do pri do?"],[967.49,"Make sacrifices They offer sacrifices and intercede with prayer."],[979.21,"Priests of the Old Testament didn't really do a lot of worship leading."],[983.45,"No, they didn't."],[984.95,"Now we do, yeah."],[987.11,"Um kings and priests."],[989.35,"Now, these people, the saints in glory in heaven, are they offering sacrifices?"],[999.51,"Like animal sacrifices."],[1001.51,"No, okay. So what does that mean they're doing?"],[1006.01,"Praying and interceding."],[1007.83,"That's the other thing that the priests do."],[1011.87,"So once again, this is very clearly saying here in Revelation, the saints in glory are praying and interceding for those on earth."],[1022.45,"This is what they're doing."],[1024.45,"So our idea of sainthood in the Orthodox Church is here in the book of Revelation."],[1030.21,"I mean, it's other places too, but it's pretty clear, here in the book of Revelation."],[1040.38,"Verse 11, then I looked, and I heard the voice of many angels around the throne, the living creatures and the elders, and the number of them was ten thousand times ten thousand, and thousands of thousands."],[1053.96,"And that's not a literal number."],[1055.24,"Okay That's gaz that's how you say gazillions in Greek."],[1061.7,"Saying with a loud voice, Worthy is the Lamb who was slain to receive power and riches and wisdom and strength and honor and glory and blessing."],[1071.22,"And every creature which is in heaven and on the earth and under the earth, and such as are in the sea, and all that are in them, I heard saying, Blessing and honor and glory and power be to him who sits on the throne and to the Lamb forever and ever."],[1087.14,"A lot of those under the earth and down in the abyss probably were not happy about having to say that, but they still kind of had to say that."],[1096.74,"The four living creatures said amen"],[1099.58,"And the 24 elders fell down and worshipped him who lives forever and ever."],[1114.54,"Okay. We're going to get into chapter 6."],[1117.42,"We're going to get into the four horsemen of the apocalypse."],[1121.02,"Fun times. Fun times."],[1125.34,"So, as we move into chapter 6, we're going to see the seals start getting opened."],[1129.98,"Okay, so what's going on with the scroll and and the seals?"],[1133.18,"It's connected to what we just saw."],[1135.64,"So, Christ has, because of his death and resurrection, he's now taken possession of the earth."],[1143.26,"That's why he can now redeem people from everywhere."],[1143.34,"'s He redeemed everybody."],[1149.67,"He now possesses them."],[1151.33,"So this scroll is sort of like a deed."],[1155.14,"Where he's taken possession."],[1157.46,"Nobody else was worthy to do it."],[1159.96,"He does it through his death and resurrection, but now he has to crack those seven seals."],[1165.8,"And so as he takes possession of the earth."],[1170.78,"And Christ becomes the ruler of everything, what's he gonna do?"],[1175.9,"So if you've got a kingdom that's become corrupt and old, and now a good, righteous king has come in, what's he gonna do?"],[1182.78,"He's gonna clean house."],[1184.55,"He's gonna put stuff back in order."],[1186.51,"There's gonna be a reckoning now."],[1189.68,"And so what we're gonna see now as we move through Revelation, we're gonna see a series of cycles."],[1197.36,"We talked back in 1 John about how when St."],[1200.16,"John writes, he writes in this cyclical pattern."],[1203.68,"This is one of the ways we know these that the gospel and 1 John and Revelation were written by the same person, is they're all structured the same way."],[1210.8,"In this circular way."],[1212.88,"And so we're gonna see these series of sevens."],[1215.6,"There's gonna be seven seals, there's gonna be seven bowls, there's gonna be seven horns."],[1220.45,"Um, and and they're gonna cycle through."],[1223.73,"And so what we're seeing now, Christ taking possession of the earth."],[1228.69,"So St This is one of the things that's playing out in history."],[1233.13,"John is seeing these broad patterns that are playing out in history."],[1237.71,"And he's saying, so he's gonna see Christ open a seal, something's gonna happen."],[1243.31,"And the thing he describes happening, the idea is that we now, at our point here on the ground, see these things happening."],[1251.87,"And so rather than seeing them, for example, and being afraid, not knowing what's going on, despairing, we're gonna say, oh, this is a sign."],[1260.89,"Christ is taking back the world."],[1264.18,"Like it's moving ahead."],[1265.54,"That's why we're seeing these things unfold."],[1268.96,"So that's sort of the the overarching idea as we get into the seals."],[1271.04,"we get into the So now'll them fun times with uh four horsemen of the apocalypse."],[1280.6,"Spoilers for a couple minutes from now, they're ancient Canaanite gods."],[1285.56,"Okay. Uh Revelation 6, verse 1."],[1292.04,"Now I saw when the Lamb opened one of the seals, and I heard one of the four living creatures saying with a voice like thunder, come and see."],[1301.8,"There's a place where Johnny Cash reads this, and he does it so much better than me."],[1306.12,"Yeah. You didn't have to agree with me about how much better he did it than you."],[1311.64,"I mean, acknowledged."],[1313.56,"Fair, but still."],[1317.24,"And I looked and behold, a white horse"],[1321.68,"He who sat on it had a bow, and a crown was given to him, and he went out conquering and to conquer."],[1330.16,"Okay. So one of these patterns that unfolds in history is conquerors."],[1338.4,"If you studied history at all, there's a succession of those."],[1343.7,"So, but let's but let's pause here."],[1346.98,"So, if you are of the mind that what Revelation is doing is it's predicting a bunch of stuff that's going to happen at the end of the world."],[1356.74,"And so you treat, for example, this."],[1359.22,"Okay, a conqueror's gonna come."],[1361.14,"This is gonna be one of the first signs we're gonna see somebody going out and conquering"],[1366.62,"And you live in basically any era of world history."],[1370.22,"You're gonna be able to find somebody."],[1373.39,"Like right now, you could say, oh look, Putin invaded Ukraine."],[1376.59,"This is it."],[1378.05,"Or it could have been Hitler or Stalin, or it could have been Napoleon, or it could have been."],[1383.22,"Yeah. Um, Genghis Khan."],[1386.25,"I mean, there's you can keep going about you can always find somebody."],[1390.62,"Who who will fit that."],[1393.18,"That's why that whole approach doesn't work."],[1396.0,"Because the point is, all of these are repeated things."],[1399.2,"Just like St."],[1400.0,"John said in 1 John, when he talked about the An Antitichchrristist. said you've heard an Antichrist will come, already plural are popping up"],[1408.92,"He talks about there being sort of a spirit of Antichrist that's at work in the world."],[1412.85,"And that culminates somewhere."],[1414.69,"There will be an a time when Christ returns."],[1417.65,"It'll be a culmination of all of these patterns."],[1420.53,"But the patterns play out sort of over and over again."],[1424.85,"And so this first pattern is conquest."],[1442.37,"Another horse, fiery red, went out, and it was granted to the one who sat on it to take peace from the earth, and that people should kill one another, and there was given to him a great sword."],[1455.85,"So this is not necessarily conquest, but just warfare."],[1460.67,"Again, any time in history, you could find plenty of examples."],[1465.81,"Unfortunately, there's always war and slaughter and death going on."],[1473.41,"Verse 5. When he opened the third seal, I heard the third living creature say, Come and see."],[1480.13,"So I looked, and behold, a black horse, and he who sat on it had a pair of scales in his hand, and I heard a voice in the midst of the four living creatures saying, A quart of wheat for a denarius, and three quarts of barley for a denarius and do not harm the oil and wine."],[1504.01,"This is like food shortage."],[1506.27,"Like famine. Yeah, yeah."],[1509.15,"And so people."],[1510.61,"Famine, people dying of hunger."],[1513.1,"Notice the nuance though that the the hunger is not so much caused by like crop failure, bad weather, lack of rain."],[1523.6,"It's sort of human caused famine, which most famine historically and today is."],[1530.42,"Like right now, I don't know right now."],[1533.14,"Now our supply chains are all messed up."],[1535.18,"But before COVID, before COVID, every year the Earth produced enough food to feed 10 billion people."],[1542.06,"And several million people starved to death every year, even though there's only 7 billion people in the world."],[1548.38,"So there were places on Earth that wasted huge amounts of food, and other places that didn't have enough."],[1554.7,"And that's something we do, to ourselves."],[1566.92,"Verse 7. When he opened the fourth seal, I heard the voice of the fourth living creature saying, Come and see."],[1573.12,"So I looked and behold, a pale horse, and the name of him who sat on it was death. and Hades followed with him"],[1581.96,"And power was given to them over a fourth of the earth to kill with sword, with hunger, with death, and by the beasts of the earth."],[1592.68,"So uh death is obviously death."],[1598.84,"Um, and uh has Hades with him sort of in toe."],[1604.36,"And Hades um the idea here is the way Hades is depicted in some of our iconography, where it's sort of this big gaping maw."],[1616.78,"Like a serpent."],[1617.82,"So the idea here is that death is running around, sort of feeding people to Hades."],[1624.62,"Feeding people to the grave."],[1626.62,"Obviously, therefore death, has been going on."],[1630.96,"Um, now I mentioned that uh the four the four horsemen here are uh ancient Canaanite gods, and they actually are."],[1642.72,"That's where the depictions come from."],[1645.68,"The depictions come from."],[1647.2,"And they're referred to at several places in the in the Old Testament."],[1650.64,"They pop up in different places, they pop up in the Psalms."],[1654.56,"Um a lot of times it's hard to tell in the English translations because they won't they won't translate their names as names."],[1666.4,"Um so uh we pray, for example, uh in um that we be delivered from uh the arrow that flieth by day in the prayers of the sixth hour."],[1685.29,"The arrow that flieth by day is actually a reference to Reshef, which is one of these ancient Canaanite gods, uh, who shot sort of poisonous plague arrows at people."],[1697.53,"There's an early firm of Apollo that's based on him too."],[1701.45,"Um, but so to get into who these guys are in in in the Canaanite gods, you have to start at the end."],[1707.61,"That's why I waited until the end to do this."],[1709.85,"Because in sort of the Canaanite stories these are all guys who work for Mote, the god of death."],[1722.93,"So Mote was the god of death."],[1727.41,"That's where the Arabic word for death comes from."],[1730.61,"It's the same word."],[1731.81,"It's the same root."],[1734.05,"And there were no there were no temples, by the way, to Moat."],[1738.53,"You didn't like worship the god of death."],[1740.71,"Like you tried to ward get rid of him and keep him away."],[1744.09,"Um but Mote sort of had these lackeys who he sent out to sort of get people for him."],[1753.26,"One of whom was Reshef, one of whom was right."],[1756.26,"Yeah, they were related to plague and famine and uh the sword."],[1764.63,"Which was violent death."],[1767.13,"And you'll there are several places in the Old Testament where you see the sword referred to, and that's not a metaphor."],[1778.15,"When uh David is told that because of what he did with Bathsheba, the sword will never depart from his house."],[1785.51,"That's talking about what they believe to be a demonic spirit that brought about violent death."],[1793.72,"So there are also prayers of the Orthodox Church where we pray to be delivered from, among other things, the sword."],[1801.69,"Obviously, that's not literal."],[1803.21,"Like, I just don't want any stab wounds."],[1805.15,"Guns are fine, but no swords."],[1806.97,"Um, it's talking about that same thing, violent death."],[1811.47,"Violent death. And so in the Old Testament, uh, in the prophets, for example, where these figures are referred to, and where Moat is referred to, uh, the story is kind of inverted."],[1830.29,"So when you read the Canaanite stories, Moat is the god of death, is nearly all powerful for them because everything dies from their perspective."],[1841.05,"They even thought their gods could die, which means Moat's kind of the most powerful one."],[1846.7,"Because everyone and everything dies, he always wins ultimately."],[1851.32,"Um you get a very sort of dark, bleak."],[1855.96,"Most ancient Near Eastern religions are pretty dark."],[1859.78,"Uh there's not a lot of hope and like fun times ahead in the afterlife for you."],[1864.74,"Um but what happens is that there are, of course, various places where where that depict Yahweh, the God of Israel, sort of threatening Moat."],[1877.62,"A lot of things that are leading into a lot of our hymnography surrounding Pasca."],[1883.0,"Of death being defeated, by Christ."],[1888.58,"But there are also these passages dealing with Mote and with these lackeys of his that talk about God having them like on a leash."],[1900.02,"Or God forcing them to serve him."],[1909.86,"If you come at it from a certain perspective."],[1912.26,"Because a lot of people come at this from the perspective of, wait, this is saying God like sends demons at people."],[1920.62,"sound good. That doesn't"],[1921.49,"Like, that's that's just sound right."],[1925.11,"But there is the perspective of the Old Testament that St."],[1927.27,"the John's really picking up here, and that's why he's using same imagery."],[1935.47,"Is that God allows these things, he allows demons to be active in the world."],[1941.63,"He allows these things for the purpose of bringing people to repentance."],[1948.13,"But he has them on a leash, meaning they're under control."],[1950.85,"We can even kind of see this with Satan in Job."],[1955.11,"Satan comes and he can talk trash about Job to God."],[1959.13,"But if he wants to do anything to Job, he has to get God's permission."],[1965.66,"That's the idea."],[1967.87,"They, of course, the demons don't want to do good"],[1970.85,"They don't want us to repent."],[1972.15,"They hate us and want to destroy us."],[1974.37,"But God sort of uses them to accomplish his will anyway."],[1979.91,"Just like the ones under the earth couldn't avoid ultimately giving praise to God, they can't avoid ultimately serving his ends, even when they're trying to be hateful and destructive."],[1994.4,"So St. John is bringing these guys back to say two things."],[2000.56,"One is that we're gonna see these patterns."],[2005.02,"And the people who St."],[2006.14,"John originally wrote this to could see these patterns."],[2009.34,"Living at the end of the first and beginning of the second century of the Roman Empire."],[2011.9,"They could see all of these things happening around them"],[2016.72,"We can see all these things happening around us."],[2019.62,"And St. John is saying, when you see these things, you should know that this is it's it's in progress."],[2026.6,"Christ is taking the world back and setting things right."],[2029.4,"Number one. But number two, we should also know that these things are being used."],[2038.13,"These events are being allowed and being used by God to bring people to repentance."],[2044.07,"To bring them back to Christ before Christ's return."],[2049.77,"Before the end."],[2051.21,"Because there is gonna be an end, and that's also g gonnaonna. that's mark the end of our suffering"],[2056.61,"It's gonna mark the end of our troubles, the end of our trials, but it's also gonna represent the end of our opportunity to repent."],[2065.25,"And so there's always a balance there."],[2068.37,"Remember, this is why St."],[2069.65,"Peter said God was Christ was delaying returning to allow time for repentance."],[2077.41,"But there will come a time when the balance moves in the other direction and then Christ will return."],[2085.41,"And so it's not that during the time between Christ's ascension and his second coming, like he's just waiting around, or he doesn't know what's happening to us, or, or he do heesn' dot knowesn' whatt know. what we're suffering's going on in the world"],[2102.97,"He knows, he's allowing it, he's using it, and this is the purpose."],[2109.26,"So these are that's sort of the two level thing that St."],[2112.7,"John is trying to convey to us here by using this Old Testament imagery."],[2123.02,"Verse 9, when he opened the fifth seal, I saw under the altar the, souls of those who had been slain for the word of God and for the testimony which they held."],[2133.86,"Okay, so these are the martyrs."],[2137.67,"Now notice there."],[2139.59,"That sounds weird, they're under the altar."],[2141.07,"the altar. We know what is"],[2141.91,"Like they're in a hole."],[2143.23,"Well. They haven't said."],[2149.47,"But we're in this worship scene."],[2151.33,"So there has to be this altar."],[2152.95,"Presumably referring to an altar of incense, because we had the bowls of incense, remember?"],[2157.11,"So incense is being offered."],[2158.79,"Rather than animals."],[2160.2,"Um so uh in the Old Testament sacrifices, remember, they weren't allowed to drink the blood, do any of the other pagan stuff with the blood."],[2172.73,"Um, so what they were told to do with the blood to stop them from doing that is that after they uh killed the animal, they drained the blood into a bowl."],[2184.33,"the So then animal could be taken and butchered and prepared to be sacrificed."],[2190.66,"The blood was taken and poured out at the base of the altar into the ground."],[2198.71,"And so the blood, remember, is the life."],[2203.24,"So the reason the souls, the lives, of the martyrs are under the altar is it's representing their blood."],[2213.28,"The blood they shed for Christ as a sacrifice, that they essentially offered themselves as a sacrifice to God."],[2222.89,"When they were martyred."],[2228.65,"Verse 10, and they cried with a loud voice, saying, How long, O Lord, holy and true, until you judge and avenge our blood on those who dwell on the earth?"],[2239.66,"So this is reinforcing that theme we were just talking about."],[2242.64,"The martyrs are like, hey, how"],[2244.65,"Because not only did they suffer this, but people they're still getting joined by other people."],[2250.15,"They said, Lord, how long are you going to let this go on?"],[2253.52,"How long? Will this continue?"],[2257.84,"Verse 11 then a white robe was given to each of them, and it was said to them that they should rest a little while longer, until both the number of their fellow servants and their brethren, who would be killed as they were was completed."],[2273.4,"So there is gonna come a time, when there is gonna be right this reckoning, but not yet."],[2289.66,"Verse 12, I looked when he opened the sixth seal, and behold there was a great earthquake, and the sun became black as sackcloth of hair, and the moon became like blood."],[2303.74,"That's not good"],[2306.55,"Uh so if the sun becomes black."],[2311.28,"And this is not talking about the blood moon."],[2313.88,"Sorry, John Hagee."],[2315.82,"Happens all the time."],[2317.1,"Not a big deal."],[2318.78,"Um keep going."],[2321.58,"Verse 13. And the stars of heaven fell to the earth as a fig tree drops its late figs when it is shaken by a mighty wind."],[2329.42,"That's a vivid description."],[2332.58,"Then the sky receded as a scroll when it is rolled up, and every mountain and island was moved out of its place."],[2340.66,"And the kings of the earth, the great men, the rich men, the commanders, the mighty men, every slave and every free man, hid themselves in the caves and in the rocks of the mountains, and said to the mountains and rocks, fall on us and hide us from the face of him who sits on the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb."],[2357.34,"For the great day of his wrath has come, and who is able to stand."],[2361.82,"Okay. Um we get to Seal 6."],[2368.22,"This is now the cusp, sort of of Christ's return."],[2372.78,"What's all this business about?"],[2374.38,"Now, we want to read this very literally."],[2377.52,"The sun, moon, and stars."],[2378.72,"What are the sun, moon, and stars everywhere else in scripture, including the first part of the book of Revelation we read?"],[2386.48,"These are angels."],[2387.54,"These are angelic beings."],[2390.23,"And one of the one of the things we kind of forget is that, for example, in Isaiah, when it talks about the day of the Lord."],[2398.81,"The day of Yahweh, God coming to judge the earth, says he says, On that day, excuse me, I will judge, I will judge those in the heavens and the heavens, and those in the earth on the earth."],[2413.13,"There's angels getting judged too."],[2416.93,"We've got John Milton in our head, so we think that sometime back, way, way back in the long ago time."],[2423.22,"A bunch of angels fell."],[2426.02,"Like things. Yeah, went somewhere, and then the rest of the angels stayed up in heaven, and so that's already kind of done."],[2432.82,"But that's not in the scriptures, and that's not in the fathers."],[2436.18,"And John Milton's a Puritan, so you can't believe him about anything."],[2439.94,"Um kill your king."],[2442.18,"You don't even know what's gonna happen"],[2444.22,"Um so um uh, for example, uh you read uh St."],[2452.96,"Gregory the Deologist, aka St."],[2455.84,"Gregory the Great."],[2457.06,"So end of the sixth century, late antiquity."],[2460.1,"He wrote a work called the Moralia, which is a commentary on the book of Job."],[2464.1,"He says, and it talks about the angels gathering, to present themselves before God on his right hand and on his left hand."],[2471.88,"He says, those on his right hand are the elect angels, those on his left hand are the evil angels."],[2479.04,"Uh and so um that that sort of winnowing. in judgment hasn't happened yet"],[2487.24,"And so what's being depicted here under the sixth seal is that two-part judgment."],[2494.04,"It starts in heaven."],[2496.62,"God judges heaven first."],[2499.44,"Wraps it up, judges the sinful angelic beings."],[2506.85,"Who get dropped like figs."],[2509.15,"Then turns to the earth."],[2512.04,"And then when he turns to the earth, all the people on earth are like, oh, we done messed up now."],[2517.66,"Because they haven't taken advantage of this life for repentance, and now that time is at its end."],[2524.98,"And so they're trying to hide, get the mountains to fall on them and hide them."],[2529.86,"Not gonna work."],[2532.23,"Um so that's that's what's being depicted here is that same movement from Isaiah."],[2538.76,"This is now happening, sixth seal at the end."],[2542.52,"Now, as I mentioned, Revelation is the series of cycles."],[2547.96,"And what's gonna be interesting is none of these cycles are gonna, well, not none."],[2551.48,"Almost none of these cycles are gonna end."],[2554.44,"So we just got six seals."],[2556.2,"So you might be expecting, I don't think we're gonna start uh chapter seven."],[2560.52,"We're not. Um, but you may be expecting, okay, so now when when when we come back next time and we get into chapter seven, that's we're gonna he's gonna open the seventh seal."],[2570.94,"You glance ahead."],[2574.94,"No. No. Not yet."],[2579.7,"Um, so something will happen with the seventh seal."],[2584.1,"But what's gonna happen with the seventh seal is it's gonna start the next series of seven things."],[2589.0,"The seventh seal is gonna be the first part of the next deal."],[2594.89,"So um, but so we'll end, we'll end here for now, time wise."],[2602.25,"We actually did like three chapters."],[2604.65,"Yeah. I I must have had more caffeine in the original."],[2609.21,"Um so they're also kind of short chapters."],[2612.17,"So thank you everybody"],[2618.13,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2625.49,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2630.85,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":20.4,"lv":2,"h":"Revelation 4:8-11 - Worship of the creatures and elders","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>v.8</b> four living creatures: <b>six wings</b> each, <b>full of eyes</b> around and within</li><li class=\"d0\">Never rest day or night: \"<b>Holy, holy, holy</b>, Lord God Almighty, who was and is and is to come\"</li><li class=\"d1\">based on the song in <b>Isaiah's vision</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Eyes = <b>power of sight</b>, <b>awareness</b> of what's on earth</li><li class=\"d1\">four cardinal points -> over the <b>whole earth</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>v.9</b> creatures give glory, honor, thanks -> <b>24 elders</b> fall down, worship, <b>cast crowns</b> before the throne</li><li class=\"d1\">\"You are worthy, O Lord... for you <b>created all things</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Antiphonal worship</b> - <b>cherubim and humans</b> back and forth in God's throne room</li></ul>"},{"t":117.66,"lv":3,"h":"Joining the worship already in progress","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Right after John went through the door: \"<b>in the spirit</b>\" = worship language, entering <b>worship</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Point: when we worship - even <b>Lafayette, Louisiana</b>, Sunday morning - we <b>join the regularly scheduled worship already in progress</b></li><li class=\"d1\">going on in heaven <b>day and night continuously</b> - \"like plugging in\"</li><li class=\"d1\">true of <b>everyone everywhere</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Connected to God, the angels - why we mention <b>angels, saints</b> serving with us in the <b>divine liturgy</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Also <b>everyone else worshiping everywhere</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Every worship service, esp. <b>divine liturgy</b> = manifestation of <b>unity of the church through time and space</b></li></ul>"},{"t":195.18,"lv":3,"h":"After a loved one dies","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Some of our people: <b>don't come to church for a while</b> after a death</li><li class=\"d1\">\"one of the <b>silliest traditions</b> I've ever heard\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Your loved one is <b>here at the church</b> every time we worship</li><li class=\"d1\">staying home = staying <b>away</b> from the one you miss</li><li class=\"d0\">Better to be here where they are - <b>worship with them, pray for them and with them</b> - than home <b>depressed and sad</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Purpose of John: the <b>reality we can't see</b> from the ground</li><li class=\"d1\">worship in a <b>cave next to a salt mine</b> - not just huddled with candles; <b>part of heaven's worship</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Biggest cathedral (<b>Hagia Sophia</b> reopened), <b>storefront</b>, <b>living room</b> - same thing we connect to</li></ul>"},{"t":291.28,"lv":2,"h":"Revelation 5:1-5 - The sealed scroll","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Scene is set</b> - now the <b>action unfolds</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>5:1</b> scroll in the <b>right hand</b> of him on the throne, <b>written inside and on the back</b>, <b>sealed with seven seals</b></li><li class=\"d1\">normally write on <b>one side</b>, roll up to protect it - here both sides, yet rolled up</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>wax seals</b> - must break to open; show if <b>opened</b> or not</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>v.2</b> <b>strong angel</b>: \"<b>Who is worthy</b> to open the scroll and loose its seals?\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>v.3</b> no one in <b>heaven</b>, <b>earth</b>, or <b>under the earth</b> (= underworld, <b>Hades</b>) able</li><li class=\"d1\">\"thoroughness, you gotta check\"</li><li class=\"d0\">John <b>wept much</b>; one of the <b>elders</b> - doesn't say which, \"wonder if he was talking to himself\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>Do not weep</b>. Behold the <b>Lion of the tribe of Judah</b>, the <b>root of David</b>, has <b>prevailed</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Lion -> <b>Genesis</b>, early messianic prophecy; root of David = <b>Messiah</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>prevailed</b> = victory accomplished -> allows him to open the seals</li></ul>"},{"t":464.56,"lv":2,"h":"5:6-8 - The Lamb as though slain","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>v.6</b> in the midst of throne, four creatures, elders: <b>a Lamb as though it had been slain</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>seven horns, seven eyes</b> = the seven spirits of God sent into all the earth</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Same throne</b> - Lamb identified as <b>Lamb of God in John's gospel</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Lamb on the throne where God sat - Bible says \"between the throne and the four living creatures\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Both <b>Messiah and God</b>; slain = Christ <b>died and resurrected</b></li><li class=\"d1\">after resurrection kept the <b>wounds</b> - marks of his <b>victory</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>v.7</b> takes the scroll from the right hand; creatures and elders <b>fall before the Lamb</b></li><li class=\"d1\">each with a <b>harp</b> and <b>golden bowls full of incense</b> = <b>prayers of the saints</b></li><li class=\"d0\">All now worship the Lamb - again: <b>he's God</b>, not someone other</li><li class=\"d0\">Harps do show up - \"not strummed sitting on clouds\"</li></ul>"},{"t":608.82,"lv":3,"h":"Prayers of the saints","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Prayers from people on earth</b> come up before Christ <b>through the saints in heaven</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Protestant friends ask where <b>praying to saints / asking saints to pray</b> is in the Bible</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Well, here's one place\" - <b>prayers offered before God by saints in heaven</b></li><li class=\"d0\">A <b>picture</b>, not a rational argument</li><li class=\"d1\">no \"you can't approach God directly\" / \"okay to go to Jesus directly\"</li><li class=\"d1\">theme from ch. 4: <b>unity of the whole church in prayer</b></li><li class=\"d1\">joined to heavenly worship -> they pray for us, we for them - <b>all praying for each other</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Questions \"why do we have to?\" <b>proceed from a foreign way of thinking</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"maybe okay, but <b>do I have to</b>?\" - whole different approach vs. John's <b>beautiful picture of the unity of the church</b></li></ul>"},{"t":768.53,"lv":2,"h":"5:9-10 - The new song: redeemed","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>v.9</b> \"You are worthy... for you were slain and have <b>redeemed us to God by your blood</b>, out of every <b>tribe, tongue, people, nation</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">how the <b>humans</b> are up there</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Redeemed</b> = like redeeming a coupon: <b>buy back</b> - here <b>out of slavery</b></li></ul>"},{"t":816.23,"lv":3,"h":"Passover, not atonement","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">We think <b>atonement / Day of Atonement</b> (wrote dissertation on it)</li><li class=\"d1\">but NT usually talks of Christ's death and resurrection as <b>Passover</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Exhibit A</b>: presented as a <b>lamb</b> - goats at Day of Atonement, <b>lamb at Passover</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Passover: people of God <b>freed from slavery</b>; God <b>judges the gods of Egypt</b></li><li class=\"d0\">= <b>redemption language</b>: slaves to <b>sin, death, demonic powers</b> -> Christ died, rose, set them free, brought them into heaven</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Every tribe, tongue, people, nation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not just Israelites freed from Egypt</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Egyptians</b> freed from Egypt, <b>Romans</b>; even \"the dreaded 19th century Germans\"</li></ul>"},{"t":934.36,"lv":3,"h":"Kings and priests","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>v.10</b> \"made us <b>kings and priests</b> to our God, and we shall <b>reign on the earth</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Already on thrones - Christ <b>sharing his rule</b> now that he's taken it</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>reigning with Christ</b> - important at <b>Revelation 20</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Priests: <b>sacrifices</b> and <b>intercede with prayer</b></li><li class=\"d1\">OT priests didn't do much worship leading (unlike now)</li><li class=\"d0\">Saints in glory offering <b>animal sacrifices</b>? No -> <b>praying and interceding</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Clear in Revelation: <b>saints in glory pray and intercede for those on earth</b></li><li class=\"d1\">our Orthodox idea of <b>sainthood</b> is here - and other places too</li></ul>"},{"t":1040.38,"lv":3,"h":"5:11-14 - Universal praise","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>v.11</b> voice of <b>many angels</b>, <b>10,000 times 10,000</b>, thousands of thousands</li><li class=\"d1\">not a literal number - \"how you say <b>gazillions</b> in Greek\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Worthy is the Lamb</b> who was slain to receive power, riches, wisdom, strength, honor, glory, blessing\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Every creature</b> in heaven, earth, under the earth, in the sea: \"Blessing and honor... to him who sits on the throne <b>and to the Lamb</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"those <b>under the earth</b> probably weren't happy about it, but still had to\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Four creatures: <b>Amen</b>; 24 elders fall down and worship</li></ul>"},{"t":1114.54,"lv":2,"h":"The scroll as a deed; cycles of sevens","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Heading to <b>ch. 6</b> - <b>four horsemen</b> - \"fun times\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Scroll</b> = like a <b>deed</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Christ, through <b>death and resurrection</b>, took <b>possession of the earth</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why he can <b>redeem people from everywhere</b> - he now possesses them</li><li class=\"d1\">nobody else worthy; now must <b>crack the seven seals</b></li><li class=\"d0\">New righteous king over a <b>corrupt, old kingdom</b> -> <b>cleans house</b>, puts things in order - <b>a reckoning</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Series of <b>cycles</b> - as in <b>1 John</b></li><li class=\"d1\">gospel, 1 John, Revelation same author - <b>same circular structure</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>seven seals, seven bowls, seven horns</b> - they <b>cycle through</b></li><li class=\"d0\">John sees <b>broad patterns playing out in history</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Christ opens a seal, something happens - we on the ground see it</li><li class=\"d1\">not fear/despair: \"this is a <b>sign</b>\" - <b>Christ is taking back the world</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Spoiler: horsemen = <b>ancient Canaanite gods</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1285.56,"lv":2,"h":"6:1-2 - First seal: white horse","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>6:1</b> Lamb opens a seal; creature with voice like <b>thunder</b>: \"<b>Come and see</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Johnny Cash reads this much better than me\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>White horse</b>, rider with a <b>bow</b>, <b>crown given</b>, \"went out <b>conquering and to conquer</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Pattern in history: <b>conquerors</b>, a succession</li></ul>"},{"t":1346.98,"lv":3,"h":"Why the end-times-prediction reading fails","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">If Revelation <b>predicts end-of-the-world events</b>: \"a conqueror's gonna come, first sign\"</li><li class=\"d1\">any era: find someone - <b>Putin</b> in Ukraine, <b>Hitler, Stalin, Napoleon, Genghis Khan</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>that's why that whole approach doesn't work</b>\" - repeated patterns</li><li class=\"d0\">Like <b>1 John</b> on <b>Antichrist</b>: \"you've heard an Antichrist will come\" - <b>already plural</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>spirit of Antichrist</b> at work in the world</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Culminates</b> when Christ returns - but patterns <b>play out over and over</b></li><li class=\"d0\">First pattern = <b>conquest</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1442.37,"lv":2,"h":"6:3-8 - Second to fourth seals","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Red horse</b>: take <b>peace from the earth</b>, people <b>kill one another</b>, <b>great sword</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not conquest - just <b>warfare</b>; always war, slaughter, death</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>6:5 Black horse</b>: rider with <b>scales</b>; \"a quart of wheat for a <b>denarius</b>, three quarts of barley... don't harm the <b>oil and wine</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">= <b>famine</b>, people dying of hunger</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>human-caused</b> famine - not crop failure, bad weather - like most famine</li><li class=\"d1\">before COVID, earth produced food for <b>10 billion</b>; <b>millions starved</b> yearly with 7 billion people</li><li class=\"d1\">places waste huge amounts, others lack - \"we do it to ourselves\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>6:7 Pale horse</b>: name <b>Death</b>, <b>Hades followed</b></li><li class=\"d1\">power over a <b>fourth of the earth</b>: <b>sword, hunger, death, beasts</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Hades in iconography: <b>gaping maw</b> like a serpent -> Death running around <b>feeding people to the grave</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1630.96,"lv":2,"h":"The horsemen as Canaanite gods","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Depictions come from <b>ancient Canaanite gods</b> - referred to in the OT, e.g. <b>Psalms</b></li><li class=\"d1\">English translations <b>don't translate their names as names</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Prayers of the <b>sixth hour</b>: delivered from \"the <b>arrow that flieth by day</b>\" = <b>Reshef</b></li><li class=\"d1\">shot <b>poisonous plague arrows</b>; early form of <b>Apollo</b> based on him</li><li class=\"d0\">Start at the end: in Canaanite stories these work for <b>Mot</b>, god of <b>death</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Mot</b> - same root as the <b>Arabic word for death</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>no temples</b> to Mot - you ward him off</li><li class=\"d1\">lackeys sent to get people: <b>plague, famine, the sword</b> = <b>violent death</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Sword</b> in OT is <b>not metaphor</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>David</b> told after <b>Bathsheba</b>: sword never leaves his house = a <b>demonic spirit</b> bringing violent death</li><li class=\"d1\">Orthodox prayers: deliver us from the <b>sword</b> - \"I just don't want stab wounds. Guns are fine\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1811.47,"lv":3,"h":"Mot inverted: God has them on a leash","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Canaanite view: Mot <b>nearly all powerful</b> - everything dies, <b>even their gods</b></li><li class=\"d1\">everyone and everything dies, he <b>always wins</b> - <b>dark, bleak</b>, little hope in afterlife (most ancient Near East)</li><li class=\"d0\">OT <b>inverts</b> it: <b>Yahweh threatens Mot</b></li><li class=\"d1\">leads to <b>Pascha</b> hymnography - <b>death defeated by Christ</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Passages: God has Mot and lackeys <b>on a leash</b>, <b>forcing them to serve him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">objection: \"God sends demons at people?\" - doesn't sound right</li><li class=\"d0\">OT perspective John picks up: God <b>allows demons to be active</b> to bring people to <b>repentance</b> - but <b>under control</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Satan in Job</b>: talks trash but needs <b>God's permission</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Demons don't want us to repent - <b>hate us</b>, want to destroy us</li><li class=\"d1\">God <b>uses them anyway</b> - like those under the earth can't avoid praising, can't avoid <b>serving his ends</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1994.4,"lv":3,"h":"Two things John is saying","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>One</b>: we'll see these patterns</li><li class=\"d1\">original readers - end of <b>1st / start of 2nd century Roman Empire</b> - saw them around them; <b>we see them around us</b></li><li class=\"d1\">when you see them: it's <b>in progress</b> - <b>Christ taking the world back and setting things right</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Two</b>: events are <b>allowed and used by God</b> to bring people to <b>repentance</b>, back to Christ <b>before the end</b></li><li class=\"d1\">the end = end of <b>our suffering, troubles, trials</b> - but also <b>end of our opportunity to repent</b></li><li class=\"d1\">a <b>balance</b>: <b>St. Peter</b> - Christ <b>delaying</b> his return to allow repentance</li><li class=\"d1\">will come a time the balance moves the other way -> Christ returns</li><li class=\"d0\">Between ascension and second coming Christ isn't <b>waiting around</b> or <b>unaware</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>he knows, he's allowing it, he's using it</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2123.02,"lv":2,"h":"6:9-11 - Fifth seal: martyrs under the altar","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>v.9</b> under the <b>altar</b> the <b>souls</b> of those <b>slain for the word of God</b> and their testimony = <b>martyrs</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"in a hole\" - in the worship scene, <b>altar of incense</b> presumably (bowls of incense)</li><li class=\"d0\">OT sacrifice: no drinking the blood or pagan blood rites</li><li class=\"d1\">drained into a <b>bowl</b>; animal butchered; blood <b>poured out at the base of the altar</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>blood is the life</b> -> <b>souls under the altar = their blood</b></li><li class=\"d1\">they <b>offered themselves as a sacrifice</b> when martyred</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>v.10</b> \"<b>How long</b>, O Lord, holy and true, until you <b>judge and avenge our blood</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">others still being <b>added</b>; \"how long are you going to let this go on?\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>v.11</b> <b>white robe</b> to each; <b>rest a little while longer</b> until the number of fellow servants to be killed <b>is completed</b></li><li class=\"d1\">a reckoning is coming - <b>but not yet</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2289.66,"lv":2,"h":"6:12-17 - Sixth seal","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>v.12</b> <b>great earthquake</b>; sun <b>black as sackcloth of hair</b>; moon <b>like blood</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not the <b>blood moon</b> - \"sorry, <b>John Hagee</b>\" - happens all the time</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>v.13</b> stars of heaven <b>fell to earth</b> like a <b>fig tree dropping late figs</b>; sky <b>receded as a scroll</b> rolled up; every mountain and island moved</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Kings, great men, rich, commanders, mighty, slave and free</b> hide in caves, rocks: \"<b>fall on us</b>, hide us from the face of him who sits on the throne, and the <b>wrath of the Lamb</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"the great day of his wrath has come, <b>who is able to stand</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Cusp of Christ's return</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2372.78,"lv":3,"h":"Sun, moon and stars are angels","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Don't read this <b>literally</b> - sun, moon, stars = <b>angels, angelic beings</b> throughout Scripture and early Revelation</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Isaiah</b>, <b>day of the Lord</b>: \"I will judge those <b>in the heavens</b> and those <b>on the earth</b>\" - <b>angels get judged too</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>John Milton</b> in our heads: way back <b>a bunch of angels fell</b>, rest stayed - already done</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not in the scriptures, not in the fathers</b>; \"Milton's a <b>Puritan</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>St. Gregory the Great</b> (late 6th c.), <b>Moralia</b> on <b>Job</b></li><li class=\"d1\">angels present themselves: <b>right hand = elect angels</b>, <b>left hand = evil angels</b></li><li class=\"d1\">that <b>winnowing hasn't happened yet</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Sixth seal = <b>two-part judgment</b></li><li class=\"d1\">starts in <b>heaven</b>: judges sinful angelic beings - <b>dropped like figs</b></li><li class=\"d1\">then <b>the earth</b> - \"oh, we done messed up now\"; used up life's time for repentance</li><li class=\"d1\">hiding under mountains - \"not gonna work\"</li><li class=\"d1\">same movement as <b>Isaiah</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2542.52,"lv":2,"h":"Cycles that don't end; wrap-up","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Revelation = series of cycles; <b>almost none will end</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Six seals so far - <b>not starting ch. 7 tonight</b></li><li class=\"d1\">expect <b>seventh seal</b> next time - glance ahead: <b>no, not yet</b></li><li class=\"d1\">something happens at the seventh seal, but it <b>starts the next series of seven</b> - first part of the next deal</li><li class=\"d0\">Ending on time: \"<b>three chapters</b>\" - \"more caffeine\"; <b>short chapters</b></li></ul>"}],"next":"Next time: <b>chapter 7</b> - the seventh seal starts the next series of sevens"});
